{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781370663,"nonce":"jEIEL0Ywk5Wf9i6/Xy0gGXHdk1k=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFYkoqA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/261","origin":"github"},"title":"BizzyBoat sim-aware core bringup for the Massabesic sim (no config duplication)","message":"Part of rolker/unh_marine_simulation#66.\n\n## Goal\n\nAdd a **sim-aware BizzyBoat core bringup** so the non-Gazebo Massabesic sim\n(`unh_marine_simulation`) can run BizzyBoat's autonomy + nav2 stack against the boat's\n**real** config — no duplication, no drift. Mirrors `ben_project11/ben_core_launch.py`'s\nbase-config + `*_sim.yaml`-overlay pattern.\n\n## Why a new launch (not reuse `core_launch.py`)\n\n`bizzyboat_project11/launch/core_launch.py` is hardware-coupled: it wires a real FCU\n(`fcu_url: /dev/fcu:57600` via mavros), SBG INS, NTRIP, Garmin sidescan, sound-speed and\nZDA serial bridges, network monitor, GPS-RTK diagnostics, mavros frame bridges. None of\nthat exists in sim. Ben's `ben_core_launch.py` is already cleanly autonomy-only (sensors\nlive elsewhere), which is why it serves both field and sim. We add the equivalent thin\nsim-core for bizzy now; a fuller split of `core_launch.py` into autonomy-vs-hardware is a\nfollow-up.\n\n## Scope\n\n- New **`bizzyboat_project11/launch/bizzyboat_sim_core_launch.py`** — brings up only the\n  sim-shareable stack, reusing the real config files:\n  - `bizzyboat.yaml` (base, always) + new `bizzyboat_sim.yaml` (overlay, `IfCondition(is_simulator)`)\n  - `mru_transform`, `sea_surface_estimator` (map_tide), `chart_datum`\n  - `marine_autonomy/robot_core_launch.py`\n  - `publish_state_launch.py` (URDF / robot_state_publisher)\n  - `s57_grids` (harmless at chart-less Massabesic; mirrors Ben)\n  - **reuses `nav_launch.py`** for nav2 (model 240 + `nav2_overlay.yaml`) — no nav2 duplication\n  - **excludes** all hardware: mavros/FCU, SBG, NTRIP, sidescan, sound-speed, ZDA, network\n    monitor, GPS-RTK diag, mavros frame bridges\n  - helm + `asv_sim` are supplied by the sim repo's `sim_robot_launch.py` (as Ben does), not here\n- New **`bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat_sim.yaml`** — sim deltas ONLY (nav sourced from\n  `asv_sim` nav topics via `mru_transform`/`platform_sender`; sim tide-threshold for the\n  chart layer), mirroring `ben_project11/config/ben_sim.yaml`. **No copy of `nav2_overlay.yaml`.**\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] `bizzyboat_sim_core_launch.py` launches the autonomy + nav2 stack under a sim namespace with `use_sim_time`\n- [ ] `bizzyboat_sim.yaml` carries only sim deltas (no duplicated planner/costmap config)\n- [ ] No real-hardware nodes (mavros/FCU, SBG, NTRIP, sidescan, serial bridges) start\n- [ ] The sim repo (`unh_marine_simulation#66`) can include it with `is_simulator:=true`\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}